      "model": "cursor-composer",
      "width": 666,
      "height": 502,
      "content": "Design an assessment page into \"Assessment Questionaire Page\" frame for a mental healthcare company which give patinet a screening to start.\n\nCore Component: A vertical list of 17 assessment questions based on DSM-5 cross-cutting domains (e.g., mood, anxiety, mania, anger). Each question is housed in a modular 'Sphinx Card' with soft rounded corners and subtle drop shadows.\n\nInteraction: For each question, provide a horizontal 1-7 severity scale (Likert scale). Label the anchors: '1 - Not at all' to '7 - Severe/Every day.' Use custom-styled radio buttons or a segmented slider that glows softly with a 'calm teal' when selected.\n\nDecorations & Context: Include a persistent sidebar or header element that provides real-time, empathetic micro-copy (e.g., 'You're doing great, Peiyuan. Just a few more to go'). Add a subtle background decoration of a 'Sphinx' geometric watermark or a soft generative 'pulse' wave to signify the AI's active listening. \n\nGenerate any components new besides shadcn into \"Assessment Questionaire Componenets\", follow the color system in \"Sphinx Deisgn Tokens\""
    },
